From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:25:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Inline FixedMul in ARM code

The renderer runs from ITCM as ARM code and multiplies in fixed point
for every column and span. FixedMul is a macro there, a 64-bit multiply
is one instruction in ARM code. Thumb code has none and still calls the
function.
---
 doomgeneric/m_fixed.c | 2 +-
 doomgeneric/m_fixed.h | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doomgeneric/m_fixed.c b/doomgeneric/m_fixed.c
index 770738c..e0727dd 100644
--- a/doomgeneric/m_fixed.c
+++ b/doomgeneric/m_fixed.c
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@
 // Fixme. __USE_C_FIXED__ or something.
 
 fixed_t
-FixedMul
+(FixedMul)
 ( fixed_t	a,
   fixed_t	b )
 {
diff --git a/doomgeneric/m_fixed.h b/doomgeneric/m_fixed.h
index 733b290..acf1045 100644
--- a/doomgeneric/m_fixed.h
+++ b/doomgeneric/m_fixed.h
@@ -34,6 +34,12 @@ typedef int fixed_t;
 fixed_t FixedMul	(fixed_t a, fixed_t b);
 fixed_t FixedDiv	(fixed_t a, fixed_t b);
 
+// Inline in ARM code, the renderer multiplies for every column and span.
+// Thumb code has no 64-bit multiply, it calls the ARM function instead.
+#ifndef __thumb__
+#define FixedMul(a, b)	((fixed_t) (((int64_t) (a) * (b)) >> FRACBITS))
+#endif
+
 
 
 #endif
